@startuml
title SIC/XE Assembler - Mapping to the Standard Two-Pass Structure
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam activity {
  BackgroundColor #F4F7FB
  BorderColor #526579
  DiamondBackgroundColor #FFF3CD
  DiamondBorderColor #9A7B20
  StartColor #58A66A
  EndColor #D9534F
  FontColor #17212B
}
skinparam note {
  BackgroundColor #FFFBE6
  BorderColor #C6B458
  FontColor #30343B
}

start
:Assembly source text;
:Assembler.assembleDetailed(source);
:Construct one Engine for this assembly run;
:Parse each source line with parseLine();
note right
  Code: lib/sic-xe/src/Assembler/parser.cpp
  Produces a vector of Statement records.
  Parsing identifies labels, instructions, directives,
  operands and expressions; it does not assign addresses
  or emit object bytes.
end note

partition "Pass 1 - Analysis, layout, and symbols" {
  :Initialize LOC and address-space limit;
  :Visit each parsed Statement in source order;
  :Record the current LOC as Statement.address;
  :Define labels and process layout directives;
  :Determine instruction sizes from InstructionDef;
  :Advance LOC and update the high-water address;
  :Validate layout, duplicate symbols, and address limits;
}

note right
  Code: Engine::pass1(), pass1Instruction(), pass1Directive()
  State: lc_, startAddr_, highWater_, symbols_, ended_.
  Instruction sizes are known before operands are encoded.
  START / RESB / RESW / ORG affect layout; EQU is evaluated
  immediately and cannot depend on a forward symbol here.
end note

partition "Pass 2 - Synthesis and output" {
  :Visit each valid Statement in source order;
  if (Instruction?) then (yes)
    :Resolve operand expressions using the symbol table;
    :Encode format 1 / 2, SIC, or XE format 3 / 4;
  else (directive)
    :Evaluate BASE / NOBASE / END state;
    :Encode BYTE and WORD data;
  endif
  :Emit bytes at each absolute statement address;
  :Record relocation entries for relocatable values;
  :Append every statement to the assembly listing;
}

note right
  Code: Engine::pass2(), pass2Instruction(), pass2Directive()
  Expression evaluation allows forward references in pass 2.
  Format-3 selection uses PC-relative, BASE-relative, or direct
  addressing; source may force ,p or ,b. Format 4 records a
  5-half-byte relocation for relocatable targets.
end note

:Build AssemblyResult;
:Return sparse CodeMemory and AssemblyInfo;
note right
  AssemblyInfo contains symbols, source locations, references,
  relocations, listing, diagnostics, start address, entry point,
  and program length. assemble() wraps assembleDetailed(), saves
  the metadata, and throws AssemblyError when errors exist.
end note

:SICXE loader consumes the in-memory CodeMemory image;
stop

legend right
  **Textbook concept -> implementation**
  Symbol table: Engine::symbols_
  Opcode table: instructionSet() / findInstruction() in isa.cpp
  Literal pool: none; C'...' and X'...' are inline BYTE data
  Object program records: none; output is sparse CodeMemory
  Linker / executable: absent; relocation entries are metadata only
endlegend

@enduml
